invariant: INV-34
file: src/gcm.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh arm64-hash-count
reason: schedule_cpu returns the schedule's low byte alone, so gcm_use_eor3
  never sees CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_EOR3, which sits in the byte above it,
  and a caller that states that bit without the SHA-3 bit runs AES-GCM
  without EOR3 (docs/decisions.md 244). bin/aes_runtime_test counts the
  calls into gcm_arm64_eor3.c's entries under the AES bit with the EOR3
  bit. Only an arm64 compiler reads the line, so the script builds that
  binary for arm64 and runs it under qemu-aarch64's max model.

--- old
static uint32_t schedule_cpu(const aes_key_schedule *k) {
    return (uint32_t)k->cpu | (uint32_t)k->cpu_high << 8;
--- new
static uint32_t schedule_cpu(const aes_key_schedule *k) {
    return (uint32_t)k->cpu;
